    "category_name": "Computer & IT Skills",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Understand Enter, Backspace, Delete, Shift, Ctrl, Alt, the Windows key, Tab, Esc and the function keys, and switch between Arabic and English typing.",
    "content": "# Lesson 05: A Tour of the Keyboard: Special Keys You Should Know\n\nMost people use only the letters and the space bar. The special keys around the edges are where the real speed is. This lesson explains what each one does so the shortcuts in later lessons make sense.\n\n## 1. The keys around the letters\n\n| Key | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Enter** | Confirms, opens, or starts a new line |\n| **Backspace** | Deletes the character to the **left** of the cursor |\n| **Delete** | Deletes the character to the **right** of the cursor, or the selected file |\n| **Shift** | Capital letters and the top symbol on a key (`!`, `@`, `?`) |\n| **Caps Lock** | Types everything in CAPITALS until you press it again |\n| **Tab** | Moves to the next box in a form; indents text |\n| **Esc** | Cancels or closes a menu / exits full screen |\n| **Ctrl** and **Alt** | Used together with other keys for shortcuts |\n| **Windows key** | Opens Start; used in many Windows shortcuts |\n| **Arrow keys** | Move the cursor or selection |\n| **Home / End** | Jump to the start / end of a line |\n| **Page Up / Page Down** | Move one screen up or down |\n| **F1-F12** | Function keys - F1 help, F2 rename, F5 refresh, F11 full screen |\n\nOn many laptops the F keys share space with volume and brightness; hold the **Fn** key to use the F function.\n\n## 2. Typing in Arabic and English\n1. Add a language: **Settings > Time & language > Language & region > Add a language** (for example *Arabic (Saudi Arabia)*).\n2. Switch while typing: **Windows key + Space** (or **Alt + Shift**).\n3. The indicator in the system tray changes between **ENG** and **AR**.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If you type and get Arabic letters when you wanted English (or the opposite), you are in the wrong language. Press **Windows key + Space** and retype.\n\n## 3. Worked examples\n### Example 1: Fixing a typo quickly\nYou typed `Helo world` and the cursor is at the end. Press **Ctrl + Left arrow** twice to jump back word by word, then the right arrow to place the cursor after the `l` and type another `l`. **Ctrl + Backspace** deletes a whole word at once.\n\n### Example 2: Filling a form without the mouse\nClick in the first box (Name), type your name, press **Tab** to jump to *Email*, type it, press **Tab** again, and finally **Enter** to submit. **Shift + Tab** goes back one box.\n\n### Example 3: Typing symbols\n- `@` = **Shift + 2**\n- `%` = **Shift + 5**\n- `_` (underscore) = **Shift + -** (minus key)\n- `#` = **Shift + 3**\n\n## 4. Common mistakes\n- **Caps Lock left on** - your password \"does not work\". Check the Caps Lock light.\n- **Pressing Delete when you meant Backspace** - remember: Backspace goes left, Delete goes right.\n- **Using the space bar to line up text.** Use **Tab** or a table instead.\n\n## 5. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Open Notepad (Windows key, type `notepad`, Enter).\n2. Type: `My email is name@example.com and the discount is 15%!`\n3. Without the mouse, move to the beginning of the line and delete the first word `My` using one shortcut.\n4. Switch to Arabic, type your name in Arabic, then switch back to English.\n5. Press **F11** in your web browser and then **Esc**/**F11** to leave full screen.\n\n:::solution\n2. Use **Shift + 2** for `@`, **Shift + 5** for `%` and **Shift + 1** for `!`.\n3. Press **Home** to jump to the start of the line. Then press **Ctrl + Delete** to delete the word to the right (`My `). (Alternatively, press **Ctrl + Right arrow** once and then **Ctrl + Backspace**.)\n4. Press **Windows key + Space** (the tray shows *AR*), type your name, press **Windows key + Space** again to return to *ENG*. If Arabic is not available, add it first in **Settings > Time & language > Language & region**.\n5. **F11** makes the browser fill the whole screen; press **F11** again to return. On some laptops you need **Fn + F11**.\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- Backspace deletes left, Delete deletes right; **Ctrl** makes both delete whole words.\n- **Tab** moves between form boxes; **Shift + Tab** goes back.\n- **Windows key + Space** switches between Arabic and English.\n",
